            <ArticleTitle>Continuous axillary nerve block for chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Continuous axillary nerve block was used to relieve pain after a chemical burn to the arm in a child on mechanical ventilation after liver transplantation. The analgesia was sufficient to replace parenteral analgesia and allow extubation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
